वल्ह् (also written बल्ह्; cf. √ बर्ह्) cl. 1. Ā. वल्हते to be excellent, Dhātup. xvi, 38;
to speak;
to kill;
to hurt;
 ‘to give’ or ‘to cover’ (दान v.l. छादन), ib. 40;
 cl. 10. P. वल्हयति, ‘to speak’ or ‘to shine’ (भाषार्थे, or भासार्थे), Dhātup. xxxiii, 97.
